{"title": "Show HN: Markov Chains for Programmers – free book (2nd ed.) with C code", "link": "https://github.com/czekster/markov", "summary": "<p>I have just finished reviewing the 2nd edition for my Markov Chains book.<p>This for programmers who want Markov chains explained through code, not proofs. You build chains as matrices and solve them in C: power method, steady state for DTMCs/CTMCs, simulation to check the numbers.<p>2nd edition just out: errata fixed, new material on uniformised/embedded\nDTMCs, and the code now has tests and CI.<p>Repo has the PDF (CC BY), C solutions (GPLv3), and ~14 models (Land of Oz,\nmouse maze, a Shakespeare sonnet...) also in PRISM, MATLAB and Excel.<p>Errata and feedback welcome.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50099490\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50099490</a></p>\n<p>Points: 2</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-10-15T05:19:48+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "Show HN: Markov Chains for Programmers – free book (2nd ed.) with C code", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://github.com/czekster/markov", "published_at": "2026-10-15T05:19:48+00:00", "summary": "<p>I have just finished reviewing the 2nd edition for my Markov Chains book.<p>This for programmers who want Markov chains explained through code, not proofs. You build chains as matrices and solve them in C: power method, steady state for DTMCs/CTMCs, simulation to check the numbers.<p>2nd edition just out: errata fixed, new material on uniformised/embedded\nDTMCs, and the code now has tests and CI.<p>Repo has the PDF (CC BY), C solutions (GPLv3), and ~14 models (Land of Oz,\nmouse maze, a Shakespeare sonnet...) also in PRISM, MATLAB and Excel.<p>Errata and feedback welcome.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50099490\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50099490</a></p>\n<p>Points: 2</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>"}}, "logged_at": "2026-10-15T05:37:21.226314+00:00"}
